## Problem : Compressed the String

## Problem Statement :

Write a program to do basic string compression. For a character which is consecutively repeated more than once, replace consecutive duplicate occurrences with the count of repetitions.

Example:
If a string has 'x' repeated 5 times, replace this "xxxxx" with "x5".
The string is compressed only when the repeated character count is more than 1.

## Example:

Sample Input 1:
aaabbccdsa
Sample Output 1:
a3b2c2dsa
Explanation for Sample Output 1:
In the given string 'a' is repeated 3 times, 'b' is repeated 2 times, 'c' is repeated 2 times and 'd', 's' and 'a' and occuring 1 time hence no compression for last 3 characters.
Sample Input 2:
aaabbcddeeeee
Sample Output 2:
a3b2cd2e5

## Appproach : Optimal Approach (Two Pointer)

I use two pointers, i and j.
Pointer i marks the beginning of the current group of consecutive characters.
Pointer j moves forward to count how many times the current character repeats consecutively.
Once a different character is found (or the end of the string is reached), I append the current character to the result. If its frequency is greater than 1, I also append the count.
Then I move i directly to j to start processing the next group.
Since both pointers only move forward and never revisit processed characters, each character is processed only once.


## code :

public class Solution {
	public static String getCompressedString(String str) {
		// Write your code here.

       //  String compressed = "";
         StringBuilder compressed = new StringBuilder();

             int i =0;
         while(i < str.length()){
            int count = 1;
            char ch = str.charAt(i);
            int j = i + 1;
            for( j = i + 1; j < str.length(); j++){
               if(str.charAt(j) == ch){
                  count++;
               }
               else{
                 
                  if(count > 1){
                         compressed.append(ch);
                         compressed.append(count);
                  }
                  else{
                   compressed.append(ch);
                        
                   }
              break;
            }

              
         }
               if(j == str.length())
               {
                  
                if(count > 1){
                      compressed.append(ch);
                         compressed.append(count);
                  }
                  else{
                   
                     compressed.append(ch);
               
                   }
               
                   }
               
             i = j;
         }
         return compressed.toString();


   }
}

## Complexity :

TC : O(n)
SC : O(n)
